/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 1 Samuel chapters 16-20
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("1samuel", [
{n:16, name:"David Anointed King", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 16:7",verse:"But the LORD said unto Samuel, Look not on his countenance, or on the height of his stature; because I have refused him: for the LORD seeth not as man seeth; for man looketh on the outward appearance, but the LORD looketh on the heart."}, facts:["Did you know the famous line 'man looketh on the outward appearance, but the LORD looketh on the heart' was spoken here, when Samuel nearly anointed the impressive Eliab (1 Samuel 16:7)?","Did you know David was the youngest of eight sons, and his own father left him out in the field when Samuel came to choose a king (1 Samuel 16:10-11)?","Did you know David first served Saul not as a warrior but as a harp player, and the king loved him and made him his armourbearer (1 Samuel 16:21-23)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did God ask Samuel about mourning for Saul?", options:["How long wilt thou mourn for Saul, seeing I have rejected him from reigning over Israel?","Why do you weep when I have chosen another?","Will you fast forty days for Saul?","Shall I restore Saul if you plead?"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:1",verse:"And the LORD said unto Samuel, How long wilt thou mourn for Saul, seeing I have rejected him from reigning over Israel? fill thine horn with oil, and go, I will send thee to Jesse the Bethlehemite: for I have provided me a king among his sons.", insight:"God gently rebuked Samuel's grief; mourning what God has set aside keeps you from the new thing He is doing."},
{q:"Why was Samuel afraid to go to Bethlehem?", options:["If Saul hear it, he will kill me","He feared the elders would drive him away","He dreaded crossing the Philistine border","He feared Jesse would refuse him"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:2",verse:"And Samuel said, How can I go? if Saul hear it, he will kill me. And the LORD said, Take an heifer with thee, and say, I am come to sacrifice to the LORD.", insight:"Even prophets feel fear; Samuel's trembling did not disqualify him, it sent him back to God for a plan."},
{q:"What cover did God give Samuel for his journey?", options:["Take an heifer with thee, and say, I am come to sacrifice to the LORD","Travel by night in disguise","Say he came to judge the city","Bring an escort of soldiers"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:2",verse:"And Samuel said, How can I go? if Saul hear it, he will kill me. And the LORD said, Take an heifer with thee, and say, I am come to sacrifice to the LORD.", insight:"God gave Samuel both courage and cover; a sacrifice was true worship, and it opened the door for the anointing."},
{q:"How did the elders of Bethlehem receive Samuel?", options:["They trembled at his coming, and said, Comest thou peaceably?","They welcomed him with a feast","They refused to open the gates","They demanded he leave at once"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:4",verse:"And Samuel did that which the LORD spake, and came to Bethlehem. And the elders of the town trembled at his coming, and said, Comest thou peaceably?", insight:"A prophet's arrival made a town tremble; the word of the Lord should still stir us when it comes."},
{q:"What did Samuel answer the trembling elders?", options:["Peaceably: I am come to sacrifice unto the LORD","I come to appoint your new governor","I come to collect the tithe","I come to warn of war"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:5",verse:"And he said, Peaceably: I am come to sacrifice unto the LORD: sanctify yourselves, and come with me to the sacrifice. And he sanctified Jesse and his sons, and called them to the sacrifice.", insight:"Peaceably. When God sends His servant, the errand is mercy even when it looks fearful."},
{q:"Whom did Samuel first think was surely the LORD's anointed?", options:["Eliab, when he looked on his countenance","Abinadab, the second born","Shammah, the strongest","Jesse, the father of the house"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:6",verse:"And it came to pass, when they were come, that he looked on Eliab, and said, Surely the LORD’S anointed is before him.", insight:"Samuel was sure about Eliab and surely wrong; first impressions are a poor anointing oil."},
{q:"What did God teach Samuel about choosing a king?", options:["Look not on his countenance or height; man looketh on the outward appearance, but the LORD looketh on the heart","Always choose the eldest son","Choose the tallest and strongest","Let the elders vote"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:7",verse:"But the LORD said unto Samuel, Look not on his countenance, or on the height of his stature; because I have refused him: for the LORD seeth not as man seeth; for man looketh on the outward appearance, but the LORD looketh on the heart.", insight:"God looks at the heart while we measure height; ask Him to train your eyes to see as He sees."},
{q:"How many of Jesse's sons passed before Samuel without being chosen?", options:["Seven","Three","Five","Nine"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:10",verse:"Again, Jesse made seven of his sons to pass before Samuel. And Samuel said unto Jesse, The LORD hath not chosen these.", insight:"Seven sons paraded past, and God said no to each; when God passes over the obvious, wait for the hidden one."},
{q:"Where was David while his brothers stood before Samuel?", options:["Keeping the sheep","Fighting in Saul's army","Serving at the tabernacle","Trading in Bethlehem"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:11",verse:"And Samuel said unto Jesse, Are here all thy children? And he said, There remaineth yet the youngest, and, behold, he keepeth the sheep. And Samuel said unto Jesse, Send and fetch him: for we will not sit down till he come hither.", insight:"The future king was in the field with sheep; God often finds His leaders at their ordinary work."},
{q:"What did Samuel say when he heard one son was missing?", options:["Send and fetch him: for we will not sit down till he come hither","Choose the best of these seven","Let the youngest stay in the field","We will wait until tomorrow"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:11",verse:"And Samuel said unto Jesse, Are here all thy children? And he said, There remaineth yet the youngest, and, behold, he keepeth the sheep. And Samuel said unto Jesse, Send and fetch him: for we will not sit down till he come hither.", insight:"We will not sit down till he come; heaven pauses for the one God has chosen."},
{q:"What did David look like when he came in?", options:["Ruddy, and withal of a beautiful countenance, and goodly to look to","Tall and battle scarred","Old and weathered","Small and sickly"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:12",verse:"And he sent, and brought him in. Now he was ruddy, and withal of a beautiful countenance, and goodly to look to. And the LORD said, Arise, anoint him: for this is he.", insight:"Ruddy and goodly to look on, yet it was the heart God had seen first; beauty was the bonus, not the basis."},
{q:"What did the LORD say the moment David appeared?", options:["Arise, anoint him: for this is he","This boy will serve in my house","Send him back to the flock","Let him stand among the servants"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:12",verse:"And he sent, and brought him in. Now he was ruddy, and withal of a beautiful countenance, and goodly to look to. And the LORD said, Arise, anoint him: for this is he.", insight:"This is he. When God points, obey quickly; Samuel did not ask for a second opinion."},
{q:"Where did Samuel anoint David?", options:["In the midst of his brethren","Alone in the pasture","Before Saul's court","At the altar in secret"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:13",verse:"Then Samuel took the horn of oil, and anointed him in the midst of his brethren: and the Spirit of the LORD came upon David from that day forward. So Samuel rose up, and went to Ramah.", insight:"Anointed in front of his brothers, all passed over; God's favor does not need privacy to be real."},
{q:"What came upon David from that day forward?", options:["The Spirit of the LORD came upon David from that day forward","A crown was set on his head","He was made captain of the army","The elders bowed down to him"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:13",verse:"Then Samuel took the horn of oil, and anointed him in the midst of his brethren: and the Spirit of the LORD came upon David from that day forward. So Samuel rose up, and went to Ramah.", insight:"The Spirit came and stayed; anointing is not a moment but a dwelling."},
{q:"What departed from Saul?", options:["The Spirit of the LORD departed from Saul","His royal crown","His army's loyalty","His sons' respect"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:14",verse:"But the Spirit of the LORD departed from Saul, and an evil spirit from the LORD troubled him.", insight:"The Spirit who came to David left Saul; you cannot grieve the Spirit and keep His presence."},
{q:"What troubled Saul after the Spirit departed?", options:["An evil spirit from the LORD troubled him","A burning fever","Dreams of war","Grief for his kingdom"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:14",verse:"But the Spirit of the LORD departed from Saul, and an evil spirit from the LORD troubled him.", insight:"An empty throne in the heart invites dark tenants; keep the Spirit, and keep your peace."},
{q:"What remedy did Saul's servants suggest?", options:["Seek out a man who is a cunning player on an harp","Offer a sacrifice every morning","Send for physicians from Egypt","March to war at once"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:16",verse:"Let our lord now command thy servants, which are before thee, to seek out a man, who is a cunning player on an harp: and it shall come to pass, when the evil spirit from God is upon thee, that he shall play with his hand, and thou shalt be well.", insight:"Music for a troubled mind; God soothes kings through shepherds' songs."},
{q:"How did one servant describe David?", options:["Cunning in playing, a mighty valiant man, a man of war, prudent in matters, a comely person, and the LORD is with him","A poor shepherd with no training","A scribe skilled in the law","A merchant's son from Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:18",verse:"Then answered one of the servants, and said, Behold, I have seen a son of Jesse the Bethlehemite, that is cunning in playing, and a mighty valiant man, and a man of war, and prudent in matters, and a comely person, and the LORD is with him.", insight:"The LORD is with him, the last and greatest item on the list; every other gift is small beside that one."},
{q:"What did Jesse send with David to Saul?", options:["An ass laden with bread, and a bottle of wine, and a kid","Gold and silver vessels","A coat of mail and a sword","Ten cheeses for the captain"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:20",verse:"And Jesse took an ass laden with bread, and a bottle of wine, and a kid, and sent them by David his son unto Saul.", insight:"Bread, wine, and a kid; a father's simple gifts carried his son into the palace."},
{q:"What happened when David played the harp for Saul?", options:["Saul was refreshed, and was well, and the evil spirit departed from him","Saul fell into a deep sleep","The whole court fled in fear","Saul commanded him to stop playing"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 16:23",verse:"And it came to pass, when the evil spirit from God was upon Saul, that David took an harp, and played with his hand: so Saul was refreshed, and was well, and the evil spirit departed from him.", insight:"Music drove the darkness out; worship is warfare, and a harp can be a sword."}
]},
{n:17, name:"David and Goliath", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 17:45",verse:"Then said David to the Philistine, Thou comest to me with a sword, and with a spear, and with a shield: but I come to thee in the name of the LORD of hosts, the God of the armies of Israel, whom thou hast defied."}, facts:["Did you know Goliath's coat of mail weighed five thousand shekels of brass, armor heavier than most grown men (1 Samuel 17:5)?","Did you know David's words 'the battle is the LORD'S' come from his speech to Goliath in this chapter (1 Samuel 17:47)?","Did you know David carried Goliath's head to Jerusalem and kept the giant's armor in his own tent (1 Samuel 17:54)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where did the Philistines gather for battle?", options:["At Socoh in Judah, pitching between Socoh and Azekah, in Ephesdammim","At the gates of Jerusalem","Beside the Jordan river","In the valley of Rephaim"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:1",verse:"Now the Philistines gathered together their armies to battle, and were gathered together at Shochoh, which belongeth to Judah, and pitched between Shochoh and Azekah, in Ephes-dammim.", insight:"They camped on Judah's soil; when the enemy pitches in your territory, remember whose land it is."},
{q:"Where did Saul and Israel pitch against them?", options:["By the valley of Elah","On the plains of Jericho","At Mizpeh","In the wilderness of Ziph"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:2",verse:"And Saul and the men of Israel were gathered together, and pitched by the valley of Elah, and set the battle in array against the Philistines.", insight:"Two armies, one valley between; the valley of Elah became a valley of decision."},
{q:"Who was the Philistine champion?", options:["Goliath, of Gath","Ishbibenob, of Gaza","Lahmi, of Ekron","Sippai, of Ashdod"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:4",verse:"And there went out a champion out of the camp of the Philistines, named Goliath, of Gath, whose height was six cubits and a span.", insight:"Goliath of Gath; the enemy always sends his biggest fear first."},
{q:"How tall was Goliath?", options:["Six cubits and a span","Four cubits","Ten cubits","Seven full cubits"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:4",verse:"And there went out a champion out of the camp of the Philistines, named Goliath, of Gath, whose height was six cubits and a span.", insight:"Six cubits and a span, near ten feet; Israel measured the giant, David measured his God."},
{q:"How heavy was Goliath's coat of mail?", options:["Five thousand shekels of brass","One thousand shekels","Six hundred shekels","Three thousand shekels"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:5",verse:"And he had an helmet of brass upon his head, and he was armed with a coat of mail; and the weight of the coat was five thousand shekels of brass.", insight:"Five thousand shekels of brass; all that metal could not stop one smooth stone."},
{q:"What other brass armor did Goliath wear?", options:["Greaves upon his legs, and a target of brass between his shoulders","A breastplate of iron and brass boots","A brass shield strapped to his arm","Brass gauntlets and a visor"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:6",verse:"And he had greaves of brass upon his legs, and a target of brass between his shoulders.", insight:"Head to foot in brass; when a man trusts his armor, he has already lost the battle that matters."},
{q:"What was Goliath's spear like?", options:["Its staff was like a weaver's beam, and its head weighed six hundred shekels of iron","A short javelin for throwing","A spear of wood with a bronze tip","A pike taller than a house"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:7",verse:"And the staff of his spear was like a weaver’s beam; and his spear’s head weighed six hundred shekels of iron: and one bearing a shield went before him.", insight:"A weaver's beam for a spear shaft; the weapons of the proud are made for show, not for standing."},
{q:"What were the terms of Goliath's challenge?", options:["One man would fight him alone, and the loser's nation would serve the winner","Both armies would charge at dawn","Israel must pay tribute of gold","The kings would wrestle for the crown"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:9",verse:"If he be able to fight with me, and to kill me, then will we be your servants: but if I prevail against him, and kill him, then shall ye be our servants, and serve us.", insight:"One fight to decide two nations; God loves to settle big things through single acts of faith."},
{q:"How did Saul and all Israel react to Goliath's words?", options:["They were dismayed, and greatly afraid","They laughed at his boasting","They sent for David at once","They marched out to meet him"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:11",verse:"When Saul and all Israel heard those words of the Philistine, they were dismayed, and greatly afraid.", insight:"Dismayed and greatly afraid; fear spreads faster than faith when no one answers the giant."},
{q:"For how many days did Goliath defy Israel?", options:["Forty days, morning and evening","Seven days","Thirty days","Twelve days"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:16",verse:"And the Philistine drew near morning and evening, and presented himself forty days.", insight:"Forty days, twice a day; the enemy repeats his taunts until someone believes God instead."},
{q:"What was David to carry to the captain of the thousand?", options:["Ten cheeses","Ten loaves of bread","An ephah of parched corn","A bottle of wine"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:18",verse:"And carry these ten cheeses unto the captain of their thousand, and look how thy brethren fare, and take their pledge.", insight:"Ten cheeses; the greatest battle of David's life began as a delivery errand."},
{q:"What did the king promise the man who killed Goliath?", options:["Great riches, his daughter to wife, and his father's house free in Israel","The throne after Saul","Command of the whole army","Half the spoil of the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:25",verse:"And the men of Israel said, Have ye seen this man that is come up? surely to defy Israel is he come up: and it shall be, that the man who killeth him, the king will enrich him with great riches, and will give him his daughter, and make his father’s house free in Israel.", insight:"Riches, a princess, and freedom; men offered rewards while God offered victory."},
{q:"How did Eliab greet David at the camp?", options:["His anger was kindled, and he accused David of pride and naughtiness of heart","He embraced his youngest brother","He asked David to carry water","He praised David for coming"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:28",verse:"And Eliab his eldest brother heard when he spake unto the men; and Eliab’s anger was kindled against David, and he said, Why camest thou down hither? and with whom hast thou left those few sheep in the wilderness? I know thy pride, and the naughtiness of thine heart; for thou art come down that thou mightest see the battle.", insight:"His own brother called him proud; sometimes the hardest opposition comes from your own house."},
{q:"What did David answer Eliab?", options:["What have I now done? Is there not a cause?","I will return to Bethlehem at once","Forgive me, my brother","I came only to bring bread"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:29",verse:"And David said, What have I now done? Is there not a cause?", insight:"Is there not a cause? When God's honor is mocked, there is always a cause."},
{q:"What did David say to Saul?", options:["Let no man's heart fail because of him; thy servant will go and fight with this Philistine","I will pray while the army fights","Send Jonathan in my place","Let us retreat to the hills"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:32",verse:"And David said to Saul, Let no man’s heart fail because of him; thy servant will go and fight with this Philistine.", insight:"Let no man's heart fail; one believing voice can steady a whole trembling army."},
{q:"What past victories gave David confidence?", options:["He had slain both a lion and a bear guarding his father's sheep","He had killed a wolf and a leopard","He had beaten two Philistine raiders","He had wrestled a wild ox"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:36",verse:"Thy servant slew both the lion and the bear: and this uncircumcised Philistine shall be as one of them, seeing he hath defied the armies of the living God.", insight:"A lion and a bear in private prepared him for a giant in public; God trains you in secret for the stage."},
{q:"Why did David take off Saul's armor?", options:["He had not proved them","The helmet was too heavy","It belonged to the king","The straps were broken"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:39",verse:"And David girded his sword upon his armour, and he assayed to go; for he had not proved it. And David said unto Saul, I cannot go with these; for I have not proved them. And David put them off him.", insight:"I have not proved them; borrowed armor never fits a calling God gave you."},
{q:"What weapons did David choose instead?", options:["Five smooth stones from the brook, his sling, and his staff","A spear and a shield","A bow with arrows","Two short swords"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:40",verse:"And he took his staff in his hand, and chose him five smooth stones out of the brook, and put them in a shepherd’s bag which he had, even in a scrip; and his sling was in his hand: and he drew near to the Philistine.", insight:"Five smooth stones; God does His greatest work with the simplest tools in surrendered hands."},
{q:"In whose name did David say he came against Goliath?", options:["In the name of the LORD of hosts, the God of the armies of Israel","In the name of the king of Israel","In his own name as a shepherd","In the name of the tribe of Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:45",verse:"Then said David to the Philistine, Thou comest to me with a sword, and with a spear, and with a shield: but I come to thee in the name of the LORD of hosts, the God of the armies of Israel, whom thou hast defied.", insight:"The name of the LORD of hosts; David brought no sword to the fight, only the greatest name in heaven and earth."},
{q:"How did David finish Goliath?", options:["He stood upon him, took Goliath's own sword, and cut off his head","He called the army to stone him","He bound him and brought him to Saul alive","He let the Philistines carry him away"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 17:51",verse:"Therefore David ran, and stood upon the Philistine, and took his sword, and drew it out of the sheath thereof, and slew him, and cut off his head therewith. And when the Philistines saw their champion was dead, they fled.", insight:"The giant's own sword finished him; God turns the enemy's weapons against him."}
]},
{n:18, name:"Saul's Jealousy", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 18:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when he had made an end of speaking unto Saul, that the soul of Jonathan was knit with the soul of David, and Jonathan loved him as his own soul."}, facts:["Did you know Jonathan sealed his covenant by giving David his own robe, sword, bow, and girdle, the very gear of a prince (1 Samuel 18:4)?","Did you know Saul hurled his javelin at David twice in this chapter, and David escaped both times (1 Samuel 18:11)?","Did you know David doubled Saul's deadly dowry, bringing back two hundred Philistine foreskins instead of the hundred demanded (1 Samuel 18:25-27)?"], questions:[
{q:"What happened between Jonathan and David when David returned from the battle?", options:["The soul of Jonathan was knit with the soul of David, and Jonathan loved him as his own soul","Jonathan challenged David to a contest","Jonathan asked David to leave the court","Jonathan warned David to fear Saul"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when he had made an end of speaking unto Saul, that the soul of Jonathan was knit with the soul of David, and Jonathan loved him as his own soul.", insight:"Soul knit to soul; God gives friendships that feel like kinship, and they come as gifts."},
{q:"What did Saul do with David that day?", options:["He took him, and would let him go no more home to his father's house","He sent him back to Bethlehem","He made him a priest","He gave him a house in Gibeah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:2",verse:"And Saul took him that day, and would let him go no more home to his father’s house.", insight:"Saul kept David close; sometimes God places you near the very one who will test you."},
{q:"What did Jonathan give David to seal their covenant?", options:["His robe, his garments, his sword, his bow, and his girdle","A crown and a signet ring","Gold and silver vessels","A chariot and horses"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:4",verse:"And Jonathan stripped himself of the robe that was upon him, and gave it to David, and his garments, even to his sword, and to his bow, and to his girdle.", insight:"A prince stripped himself for a shepherd; true friendship gives its best, not its leftovers."},
{q:"What charge did Saul give David?", options:["He set him over the men of war","He made him keeper of the palace","He sent him to guard the sheep","He made him a scribe"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:5",verse:"And David went out whithersoever Saul sent him, and behaved himself wisely: and Saul set him over the men of war, and he was accepted in the sight of all the people, and also in the sight of Saul’s servants.", insight:"Set over the men of war; faithfulness in small errands leads to large commands."},
{q:"What did the women sing as the army returned?", options:["Saul hath slain his thousands, and David his ten thousands","Blessed be the king forever","David is the shepherd of Israel","The Philistines are fallen"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:7",verse:"And the women answered one another as they played, and said, Saul hath slain his thousands, and David his ten thousands.", insight:"Thousands and ten thousands; a careless song planted a bitter seed in Saul's heart."},
{q:"How did Saul take the women's song?", options:["The saying displeased him, and he was very wroth","He laughed and joined the singing","He rewarded the singers","He ignored it completely"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:8",verse:"And Saul was very wroth, and the saying displeased him; and he said, They have ascribed unto David ten thousands, and to me they have ascribed but thousands: and what can he have more but the kingdom?", insight:"Very wroth at a song; envy turns music into poison."},
{q:"What did Saul say the singers had left for David?", options:["What can he have more but the kingdom?","He shall have my daughter","He shall command my guard","He shall sit at my table"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:8",verse:"And Saul was very wroth, and the saying displeased him; and he said, They have ascribed unto David ten thousands, and to me they have ascribed but thousands: and what can he have more but the kingdom?", insight:"What can he have more but the kingdom? Jealousy always imagines the worst."},
{q:"How did Saul look at David from that day forward?", options:["Saul eyed David from that day and forward","He watched him with admiration","He avoided David's gaze","He looked on him as a son"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:9",verse:"And Saul eyed David from that day and forward.", insight:"Saul eyed David; the eye of envy watches for faults it can punish."},
{q:"What happened the day after the song?", options:["The evil spirit from God came upon Saul, he prophesied, and David played as at other times, with a javelin in Saul's hand","Saul held a feast for David","Saul sent David to the front","Saul fell ill and kept his bed"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:10",verse:"And it came to pass on the morrow, that the evil spirit from God came upon Saul, and he prophesied in the midst of the house: and David played with his hand, as at other times: and there was a javelin in Saul’s hand.", insight:"A javelin in the hand of a troubled king; when envy festers, worship itself becomes dangerous."},
{q:"What did Saul try to do to David?", options:["He cast the javelin, saying, I will smite David even to the wall","He ordered his arrest","He challenged him to a duel","He sent him into exile"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:11",verse:"And Saul cast the javelin; for he said, I will smite David even to the wall with it. And David avoided out of his presence twice.", insight:"Smite David even to the wall; rage aims at the very one God sent to soothe it."},
{q:"How many times did David escape Saul's javelin that day?", options:["Twice","Once","Three times","He was wounded once"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:11",verse:"And Saul cast the javelin; for he said, I will smite David even to the wall with it. And David avoided out of his presence twice.", insight:"Twice he dodged; God can make a javelin miss as surely as He can stop it."},
{q:"Why was Saul afraid of David?", options:["Because the LORD was with him, and was departed from Saul","Because David was stronger","Because the people loved David","Because David threatened him"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:12",verse:"And Saul was afraid of David, because the LORD was with him, and was departed from Saul.", insight:"The LORD was with him; the presence Saul lost is what frightened him most in David."},
{q:"What post did Saul give David then?", options:["He made him his captain over a thousand","He made him keeper of the armory","He sent him to Bethlehem","He made him a judge"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:13",verse:"Therefore Saul removed him from him, and made him his captain over a thousand; and he went out and came in before the people.", insight:"Captain over a thousand; Saul meant to distance David, but God meant to train him."},
{q:"How did David behave in his new place?", options:["He behaved himself wisely in all his ways, and the LORD was with him","He boasted of his victories","He plotted against Saul","He hid from the people"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:14",verse:"And David behaved himself wisely in all his ways; and the LORD was with him.", insight:"Wisely in all his ways; promotion tests character more than battle does."},
{q:"How did all Israel and Judah feel toward David?", options:["They loved him, because he went out and came in before them","They feared his ambition","They envied his favor","They ignored him"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:16",verse:"But all Israel and Judah loved David, because he went out and came in before them.", insight:"They loved him; a leader who goes out and comes in with his people wins hearts without trying."},
{q:"What did Saul offer David, and at what price?", options:["His elder daughter Merab to wife, if David would be valiant and fight the LORD's battles","His crown after his death","Half his kingdom","Command of the palace guard"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:17",verse:"And Saul said to David, Behold my elder daughter Merab, her will I give thee to wife: only be thou valiant for me, and fight the LORD’S battles. For Saul said, Let not mine hand be upon him, but let the hand of the Philistines be upon him.", insight:"A daughter for a warrior's danger; Saul's gifts always had hooks in them."},
{q:"How did David answer Saul's offer?", options:["Who am I, and what is my father's family in Israel, that I should be son in law to the king?","I accept with all my heart","Give me time to consider","I am not worthy of this honor"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:18",verse:"And David said unto Saul, Who am I? and what is my life, or my father’s family in Israel, that I should be son in law to the king?", insight:"Who am I? True greatness stays humble when the crown comes calling."},
{q:"What became of Merab?", options:["She was given to Adriel the Meholathite to wife","She married David","She remained unmarried","She fled to the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:19",verse:"But it came to pass at the time when Merab Saul’s daughter should have been given to David, that she was given unto Adriel the Meholathite to wife.", insight:"Promised to David, given to another; the word of a jealous man is wind."},
{q:"What dowry did Saul demand for Michal?", options:["An hundred foreskins of the Philistines, to be avenged of the king's enemies","A thousand shekels of gold","The head of Goliath's brother","A fortress in Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:25",verse:"And Saul said, Thus shall ye say to David, The king desireth not any dowry, but an hundred foreskins of the Philistines, to be avenged of the king’s enemies. But Saul thought to make David fall by the hand of the Philistines.", insight:"A dowry meant to kill the bridegroom; Saul plotted murder and called it marriage."},
{q:"What did David bring back instead?", options:["He slew two hundred Philistines and gave their foreskins in full tale","He brought exactly one hundred","He refused the dowry","He paid in silver"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 18:27",verse:"Wherefore David arose and went, he and his men, and slew of the Philistines two hundred men; and David brought their foreskins, and they gave them in full tale to the king, that he might be the king’s son in law. And Saul gave him Michal his daughter to wife.", insight:"Two hundred for one hundred; when men plot against you, God lets you answer with abundance."}
]},
{n:19, name:"Escape from Saul", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 19:24",verse:"And he stript off his clothes also, and prophesied before Samuel in like manner, and lay down naked all that day and all that night. Wherefore they say, Is Saul also among the prophets?"}, facts:["Did you know Michal fooled Saul's assassins with a household idol tucked in David's bed, a goats' hair pillow for its head (1 Samuel 19:13)?","Did you know every band Saul sent to seize David at Naioth ended up prophesying instead, and so did Saul himself (1 Samuel 19:20-24)?","Did you know the saying 'Is Saul also among the prophets?' is repeated here, after Saul lay prophesying all day and all that night (1 Samuel 19:24)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Saul command Jonathan and his servants?", options:["That they should kill David","That they should arrest David","That they should exile David","That they should watch David"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:1",verse:"And Saul spake to Jonathan his son, and to all his servants, that they should kill David.", insight:"Kill David; envy that began with a song had ripened into a command."},
{q:"How did Jonathan warn David?", options:["Take heed until the morning, abide in a secret place, and hide thyself","Flee to the Philistines","Hide in the palace","Go to Samuel at once"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:2",verse:"But Jonathan Saul’s son delighted much in David: and Jonathan told David, saying, Saul my father seeketh to kill thee: now therefore, I pray thee, take heed to thyself until the morning, and abide in a secret place, and hide thyself:", insight:"A true friend warns you plainly; Jonathan risked his father's wrath to save David's life."},
{q:"What did Jonathan promise to do for David?", options:["Commune with his father in the field and tell David all he saw","Fight Saul himself","Hide David in his own house","Send David to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:3",verse:"And I will go out and stand beside my father in the field where thou art, and I will commune with my father of thee; and what I see, that I will tell thee.", insight:"I will tell thee; friendship that acts in secret is still friendship that acts."},
{q:"How did Jonathan speak of David to Saul?", options:["He spake good of David unto Saul","He accused David of treason","He said nothing at all","He mocked David's fears"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:4",verse:"And Jonathan spake good of David unto Saul his father, and said unto him, Let not the king sin against his servant, against David; because he hath not sinned against thee, and because his works have been to thee-ward very good:", insight:"He spake good of David; speak well of your friends especially when it costs you."},
{q:"What did Jonathan remind Saul that David had done?", options:["He put his life in his hand and slew the Philistine, and the LORD wrought a great salvation","He paid Saul's taxes","He built Saul's palace","He spared Saul's life"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:5",verse:"For he did put his life in his hand, and slew the Philistine, and the LORD wrought a great salvation for all Israel: thou sawest it, and didst rejoice: wherefore then wilt thou sin against innocent blood, to slay David without a cause?", insight:"Sin against innocent blood without a cause; Jonathan named the sin plainly, and it stopped a king."},
{q:"What did Saul swear after Jonathan's plea?", options:["As the LORD liveth, he shall not be slain","David shall be exiled","David shall pay a fine","David shall serve me forever"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:6",verse:"And Saul hearkened unto the voice of Jonathan: and Saul sware, As the LORD liveth, he shall not be slain.", insight:"He shall not be slain; even a troubled king can be turned by truth spoken in love."},
{q:"What was David's place after Jonathan's plea?", options:["He was in Saul's presence, as in times past","He was made captain","He was sent to Bethlehem","He was given Michal"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:7",verse:"And Jonathan called David, and Jonathan shewed him all those things. And Jonathan brought David to Saul, and he was in his presence, as in times past.", insight:"As in times past; mercy restored what envy had broken, for a little while."},
{q:"What did David do in the next war?", options:["He smote the Philistines with a great slaughter, and they fled from him","He stayed in the palace","He negotiated a treaty","He lost the battle"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:8",verse:"And there was war again: and David went out, and fought with the Philistines, and slew them with a great slaughter; and they fled from him.", insight:"A great slaughter; David kept serving the king who wanted him dead."},
{q:"What came upon Saul again as David played?", options:["The evil spirit from the LORD was upon Saul, as he sat with his javelin in his hand","A spirit of prophecy","A deep and peaceful sleep","A vision of angels"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:9",verse:"And the evil spirit from the LORD was upon Saul, as he sat in his house with his javelin in his hand: and David played with his hand.", insight:"Javelin in hand while David played; the same music that once soothed him now found a harder heart."},
{q:"What happened to Saul's javelin that night?", options:["David slipped away, and Saul smote the javelin into the wall","It struck David's shoulder","It broke in Saul's hand","It fell to the floor"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:10",verse:"And Saul sought to smite David even to the wall with the javelin; but he slipped away out of Saul’s presence, and he smote the javelin into the wall: and David fled, and escaped that night.", insight:"Into the wall; God turns aimed weapons into wall decorations."},
{q:"When did David escape that night?", options:["David fled, and escaped that night","He waited until morning","He hid in the palace","He went to Jonathan's house"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:10",verse:"And Saul sought to smite David even to the wall with the javelin; but he slipped away out of Saul’s presence, and he smote the javelin into the wall: and David fled, and escaped that night.", insight:"That night; when God opens the door, do not wait for morning."},
{q:"What did Saul order against David's house?", options:["Messengers to watch the house and slay him in the morning","Guards to protect the house","A feast at the house","Tax collectors at the door"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:11",verse:"Saul also sent messengers unto David’s house, to watch him, and to slay him in the morning: and Michal David’s wife told him, saying, If thou save not thy life to night, to morrow thou shalt be slain.", insight:"Slay him in the morning; darkness plots by night what it hopes to finish at dawn."},
{q:"How did Michal warn David?", options:["If thou save not thy life to night, to morrow thou shalt be slain","Hide under the bed","Bribe the guards","Pretend to be ill"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:11",verse:"Saul also sent messengers unto David’s house, to watch him, and to slay him in the morning: and Michal David’s wife told him, saying, If thou save not thy life to night, to morrow thou shalt be slain.", insight:"To night or to morrow thou shalt be slain; love that warns is love that saves."},
{q:"How did David get out of the house?", options:["Michal let him down through a window","He walked past the guards","He climbed over the roof","He hid in a cart"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:12",verse:"So Michal let David down through a window: and he went, and fled, and escaped.", insight:"Down through a window; God uses windows when doors are watched."},
{q:"What did Michal put in David's bed?", options:["An image, with a pillow of goats' hair for his bolster, covered with a cloth","A pile of blankets","Her own cloak","A sack of grain"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:13",verse:"And Michal took an image, and laid it in the bed, and put a pillow of goats hair for his bolster, and covered it with a cloth.", insight:"An image with goats' hair for a head; desperate love invents desperate disguises."},
{q:"What did Saul command when told David was sick?", options:["Bring him up to me in the bed, that I may slay him","Send a physician","Let him rest a week","Carry him to the temple"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:15",verse:"And Saul sent the messengers again to see David, saying, Bring him up to me in the bed, that I may slay him.", insight:"Bring him in the bed; hatred does not pause for sickness."},
{q:"What did the messengers find in the bed?", options:["An image in the bed, with a pillow of goats' hair for his bolster","David fast asleep","An empty bed","Michal weeping"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:16",verse:"And when the messengers were come in, behold, there was an image in the bed, with a pillow of goats’ hair for his bolster.", insight:"An image in the bed; lies unravel the moment they are examined."},
{q:"What excuse did Michal give Saul?", options:["He said unto me, Let me go; why should I kill thee?","David overpowered me","I knew nothing of it","The guards let him pass"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:17",verse:"And Saul said unto Michal, Why hast thou deceived me so, and sent away mine enemy, that he is escaped? And Michal answered Saul, He said unto me, Let me go; why should I kill thee?", insight:"Why should I kill thee? She claimed David threatened her; fear makes even the loyal invent stories."},
{q:"To whom did David flee at Ramah?", options:["Samuel","Jonathan","The priests at Nob","The elders of Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:18",verse:"So David fled, and escaped, and came to Samuel to Ramah, and told him all that Saul had done to him. And he and Samuel went and dwelt in Naioth.", insight:"To Samuel; when the king hunts you, run to the prophet who anointed you."},
{q:"What happened when Saul himself came to Naioth?", options:["The Spirit of God came upon him; he stripped off his clothes and prophesied, lying naked all that day and night","He captured David at once","He repented and wept","He burned Naioth to the ground"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 19:24",verse:"And he stript off his clothes also, and prophesied before Samuel in like manner, and lay down naked all that day and all that night. Wherefore they say, Is Saul also among the prophets?", insight:"Stripped and prophesying all day and night; God can humble a king without lifting a sword."}
]},
{n:20, name:"The Arrow Signal", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 20:42",verse:"And Jonathan said to David, Go in peace, forasmuch as we have sworn both of us in the name of the LORD, saying, The LORD be between me and thee, and between my seed and thy seed for ever. And he arose and departed: and Jonathan went into the city."}, facts:["Did you know Jonathan and David arranged a secret arrow code: arrows falling near meant 'all is well,' arrows flying beyond meant 'flee' (1 Samuel 20:20-22)?","Did you know Jonathan made David promise kindness to his family forever, thinking of his children's future in the middle of his own danger (1 Samuel 20:14-15)?","Did you know Saul hurled his javelin at his own son Jonathan when Jonathan defended David (1 Samuel 20:33)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did David ask Jonathan when he fled to him?", options:["What have I done? what is mine iniquity? and what is my sin before thy father, that he seeketh my life?","Where can I hide?","Will you fight your father?","Shall I flee to the Philistines?"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:1",verse:"And David fled from Naioth in Ramah, and came and said before Jonathan, What have I done? what is mine iniquity? and what is my sin before thy father, that he seeketh my life?", insight:"What have I done? The innocent still ask what they did wrong; a clear conscience still seeks understanding."},
{q:"What did Jonathan first believe about his father?", options:["He will do nothing great or small without showing it to me","Saul had already forgiven David","Saul was planning a feast","Saul had left for war"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:2",verse:"And he said unto him, God forbid; thou shalt not die: behold, my father will do nothing either great or small, but that he will shew it me: and why should my father hide this thing from me? it is not so.", insight:"He will shew it me; Jonathan trusted his father more than his father deserved."},
{q:"What feast was coming the next day?", options:["The new moon","The passover","The feast of tabernacles","A wedding feast"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:5",verse:"And David said unto Jonathan, Behold, to morrow is the new moon, and I should not fail to sit with the king at meat: but let me go, that I may hide myself in the field unto the third day at even.", insight:"The new moon; God's calendar set the stage for their parting."},
{q:"What did Jonathan say would give David's absence away?", options:["Thou shalt be missed, because thy seat will be empty","The guards would report him","Samuel would tell Saul","The cooks would ask for him"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:18",verse:"Then Jonathan said to David, To morrow is the new moon: and thou shalt be missed, because thy seat will be empty.", insight:"Thy seat will be empty; sometimes absence speaks louder than presence."},
{q:"What was David's plan for the feast?", options:["Hide himself in the field unto the third day at even","Attend in disguise","Send a servant in his place","Flee to Bethlehem at once"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:5",verse:"And David said unto Jonathan, Behold, to morrow is the new moon, and I should not fail to sit with the king at meat: but let me go, that I may hide myself in the field unto the third day at even.", insight:"Hide in the field; sometimes wisdom withdraws instead of confronting."},
{q:"What excuse was Jonathan to give for David's absence?", options:["David asked leave to run to Bethlehem, for a yearly sacrifice for all the family","David was ill in bed","David was called to war","David was visiting Samuel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:6",verse:"If thy father at all miss me, then say, David earnestly asked leave of me that he might run to Bethlehem his city: for there is a yearly sacrifice there for all the family.", insight:"A yearly sacrifice; the cover was true to David's family, and it tested Saul's heart."},
{q:"How would they read Saul's answer?", options:["If he say, It is well, there is peace; if he be very wroth, evil is determined","If he laughs, all is well","If he is silent, they must flee","If he eats, David is safe"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:7",verse:"If he say thus, It is well; thy servant shall have peace: but if he be very wroth, then be sure that evil is determined by him.", insight:"Wroth or well; a man's anger often reveals what his words hide."},
{q:"What did Jonathan promise David?", options:["Whatsoever thy soul desireth, I will even do it for thee","I will give thee my crown","I will hide thee in my house","I will fight my father"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:4",verse:"Then said Jonathan unto David, Whatsoever thy soul desireth, I will even do it for thee.", insight:"Whatsoever thy soul desireth; friendship at its highest lays itself at your feet."},
{q:"What did Jonathan ask David never to cut off?", options:["His kindness from Jonathan's house for ever","His share of the spoil","The tribute of Judah","The sacrifices at Bethlehem"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:15",verse:"But also thou shalt not cut off thy kindness from my house for ever: no, not when the LORD hath cut off the enemies of David every one from the face of the earth.", insight:"Kindness for ever; Jonathan was thinking of his children while facing his own danger."},
{q:"Why did Jonathan make David swear again?", options:["Because he loved him as he loved his own soul","Because he doubted David","Because Saul commanded it","Because the priests required it"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:17",verse:"And Jonathan caused David to swear again, because he loved him: for he loved him as he loved his own soul.", insight:"As his own soul; love that deep wants its promises sealed twice."},
{q:"What signal did Jonathan plan with his arrows?", options:["He would shoot three arrows to the side, as though at a mark","He would break his bow","He would fire into the air","He would shoot at David"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:20",verse:"And I will shoot three arrows on the side thereof, as though I shot at a mark.", insight:"Three arrows; God often speaks His clearest warnings through agreed signs."},
{q:"What words would mean David was safe?", options:["Behold, the arrows are on this side of thee, take them","The arrows are lost in the grass","Go home to Bethlehem","The king is coming"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:21",verse:"And, behold, I will send a lad, saying, Go, find out the arrows. If I expressly say unto the lad, Behold, the arrows are on this side of thee, take them; then come thou: for there is peace to thee, and no hurt; as the LORD liveth.", insight:"On this side, take them; peace has a sound, and Jonathan gave it words."},
{q:"What words would mean David must flee?", options:["Behold, the arrows are beyond thee; go thy way: for the LORD hath sent thee away","The arrows are broken","Return to the palace","Wait until morning"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:22",verse:"But if I say thus unto the young man, Behold, the arrows are beyond thee; go thy way: for the LORD hath sent thee away.", insight:"Beyond thee, go thy way; the hardest word a friend can speak is the one that sends you away."},
{q:"Why did Saul say nothing the first day David was missing?", options:["He thought, He is not clean; surely he is not clean","He had forgotten David","He was ill himself","He was planning a surprise"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:26",verse:"Nevertheless Saul spake not any thing that day: for he thought, Something hath befallen him, he is not clean; surely he is not clean.", insight:"Not clean; Saul excused the absence, but his heart was already counting."},
{q:"What did Jonathan tell Saul about David?", options:["David asked leave to go to Bethlehem to see his brethren for the family sacrifice","David was sick","David had fled to Samuel","David was hunting"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:29",verse:"And he said, Let me go, I pray thee; for our family hath a sacrifice in the city; and my brother, he hath commanded me to be there: and now, if I have found favour in thine eyes, let me get away, I pray thee, and see my brethren. Therefore he cometh not unto the king’s table.", insight:"Let me see my brethren; the excuse was simple, and it drew out Saul's rage."},
{q:"How did Saul insult Jonathan?", options:["Thou son of the perverse rebellious woman","Thou traitor to the crown","Thou friend of shepherds","Thou coward of Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:30",verse:"Then Saul’s anger was kindled against Jonathan, and he said unto him, Thou son of the perverse rebellious woman, do not I know that thou hast chosen the son of Jesse to thine own confusion, and unto the confusion of thy mother’s nakedness?", insight:"Son of the perverse rebellious woman; rage insults the mother when it cannot answer the son."},
{q:"What did Saul accuse Jonathan of choosing?", options:["The son of Jesse, to his own confusion","The Philistines over Israel","Exile over the throne","War over peace"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:30",verse:"Then Saul’s anger was kindled against Jonathan, and he said unto him, Thou son of the perverse rebellious woman, do not I know that thou hast chosen the son of Jesse to thine own confusion, and unto the confusion of thy mother’s nakedness?", insight:"To thine own confusion; Saul saw Jonathan's loyalty as shame, but heaven called it glory."},
{q:"What did Saul do when Jonathan defended David?", options:["He cast a javelin at Jonathan to smite him","He wept and relented","He ordered Jonathan's arrest","He left the table"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:33",verse:"And Saul cast a javelin at him to smite him: whereby Jonathan knew that it was determined of his father to slay David.", insight:"A javelin at his own son; envy at last struck the house it lived in."},
{q:"What did Jonathan understand then?", options:["It was determined of his father to slay David","Saul was only testing him","David was already dead","Saul would forgive"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:33",verse:"And Saul cast a javelin at him to smite him: whereby Jonathan knew that it was determined of his father to slay David.", insight:"Determined to slay David; some hearts only reveal themselves when opposed."},
{q:"How did David and Jonathan part in the field?", options:["David bowed three times; they kissed one another and wept, until David exceeded","They shook hands and parted in silence","They embraced once and ran","They parted with angry words"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 20:41",verse:"And as soon as the lad was gone, David arose out of a place toward the south, and fell on his face to the ground, and bowed himself three times: and they kissed one another, and wept one with another, until David exceeded.", insight:"They wept till David exceeded; strong men weep, and God counts those tears."}
]}
]);
